- name: epy_block_1
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: "import numpy as np\nfrom gnuradio import gr\nimport struct\nimport\
      \ zlib\nimport time\nimport os\nimport inspect\nfrom collections import deque\n\
      \n# Synchronous PRBS whitening keystream matching transmitter\n_rng = np.random.RandomState(42)\n\
      WHITENING_KEY = _rng.randint(0, 256, size=2048, dtype=np.uint8)\n\nclass blk(gr.sync_block):\n\
      \    \"\"\"Robust QPSK Text Packet Deframer, Descrambler, CRC32 Verifier & Qt\
      \ GUI Display\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, log_to_file=True):\n        gr.sync_block.__init__(\n\
      \            self,\n            name='Text Packet Deframer & GUI',\n       \
      \     in_sig=[np.uint8],\n            out_sig=[]\n        )\n        self.log_to_file\
      \ = bool(log_to_file)\n        \n        # 32-symbol preamble matching transmitter\n\
      \        self.preamble = np.array([3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 3, 0, 3, 3,\
      \ 3, 3,\n                                  3, 3, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 3, 0, 3, 3,\
      \ 0, 0, 3, 0, 3], dtype=np.uint8)\n        \n        self.buffer = np.array([],\
      \ dtype=np.uint8)\n        \n        # Statistics\n        self.total_packets\
      \ = 0\n        self.crc_errors = 0\n        self.last_seq = -1\n        self.last_text\
      \ = \"\"\n        self.recent_messages = deque(maxlen=50)\n        \n      \
      \  # File Logging\n        dir_path = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\
      \ if '__file__' in locals() else '.'\n        self.log_path = os.path.join(dir_path,\
      \ 'rx_text_log.txt')\n        self.log_file = None\n        if self.log_to_file:\n\
      \            try:\n                self.log_file = open(self.log_path, 'a',\
      \ encoding='utf-8')\n                self.log_file.write(f\"\\n=== QPSK Text\
      \ Receiver Started: {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')} ===\\n\")\n       \
      \         self.log_file.flush()\n            except Exception as e:\n      \
      \          print(f\"[RX Deframer] File log init warning: {e}\")\n          \
      \      \n        # Qt GUI Widget Injection\n        self.top_block = None\n\
      \        self.status_label = None\n        self.text_display = None\n      \
      \  self.gui_timer = None\n        \n        for frame_info in inspect.stack():\n\
      \            frame = frame_info.frame\n            if 'self' in frame.f_locals:\n\
      \                val = frame.f_locals['self']\n                if hasattr(val,\
      \ 'top_grid_layout'):\n                    self.top_block = val\n          \
      \          break\n                    \n        if self.top_block:\n       \
      \     try:\n                from PyQt5.QtWidgets import QLabel, QTextEdit, QVBoxLayout,\
      \ QWidget\n                from PyQt5.QtCore import QTimer\n               \
      \ \n                self.gui_container = QWidget()\n                layout =\
      \ QVBoxLayout(self.gui_container)\n                layout.setContentsMargins(4,\
      \ 4, 4, 4)\n                layout.setSpacing(4)\n                \n       \
      \         self.status_label = QLabel(\"Waiting for QPSK signal... [Packets:\
      \ 0 | CRC Errors: 0]\")\n                self.status_label.setStyleSheet(\n\
      \                    \"background-color: #1e1e2e; color: #a6e3a1; font-size:\
      \ 14px; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px; border-radius: 4px;\"\n           \
      \     )\n                layout.addWidget(self.status_label)\n             \
      \   \n                self.text_display = QTextEdit()\n                self.text_display.setReadOnly(True)\n\
      \                self.text_display.setStyleSheet(\n                    \"background-color:\
      \ #181825; color: #cdd6f4; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; font-size: 12px;\
      \ border: 1px solid #313244; border-radius: 4px;\"\n                )\n    \
      \            self.text_display.setMinimumHeight(180)\n                layout.addWidget(self.text_display)\n\
      \                \n                # Add to GNU Radio QT GUI layout (top row)\n\
      \                self.top_block.top_grid_layout.addWidget(self.gui_container,\
      \ 0, 0, 1, 2)\n                \n                self.gui_timer = QTimer()\n\
      \                self.gui_timer.setInterval(150)\n                self.gui_timer.timeout.connect(self.update_gui)\n\
      \                self.gui_timer.start()\n                print(f\"[RX Deframer]\
      \ GUI initialized. Log file: {self.log_path}\")\n            except Exception\
      \ as e:\n                print(f\"[RX Deframer] GUI setup warning: {e}\")\n\n\
      \    def symbols_to_bytes(self, syms):\n        \"\"\"Convert array of 2-bit\
      \ symbols to bytes (4 symbols per byte)\"\"\"\n        n_bytes = len(syms) //\
      \ 4\n        byte_arr = bytearray(n_bytes)\n        for i in range(n_bytes):\n\
      \            s0 = int(syms[4*i])\n            s1 = int(syms[4*i + 1])\n    \
      \        s2 = int(syms[4*i + 2])\n            s3 = int(syms[4*i + 3])\n    \
      \        byte_arr[i] = (s0 << 6) | (s1 << 4) | (s2 << 2) | s3\n        return\
      \ bytes(byte_arr)\n\n    def update_gui(self):\n        if not self.status_label\
      \ or not self.text_display:\n            return\n            \n        total\
      \ = self.total_packets\n        errs = self.crc_errors\n        total_attempts\
      \ = total + errs\n        success_pct = (total / total_attempts * 100.0) if\
      \ total_attempts > 0 else 100.0\n        \n        status_text = (\n       \
      \     f\"Received Packets: {total:,}  |  CRC Errors: {errs:,}  |  \"\n     \
      \       f\"Pass Rate: {success_pct:.1f}%  |  Last Seq: #{self.last_seq}\"\n\
      \        )\n        self.status_label.setText(status_text)\n        \n     \
      \   lines = []\n        while self.recent_messages:\n            lines.append(self.recent_messages.popleft())\n\
      \            \n        if lines:\n            self.text_display.append(\"\\\
      n\".join(lines))\n            sb = self.text_display.verticalScrollBar()\n \
      \           sb.setValue(sb.maximum())\n\n    def work(self, input_items, output_items):\n\
      \        in_syms = input_items[0]\n        if len(in_syms) == 0:\n         \
      \   return 0\n            \n        data = np.concatenate([self.buffer, in_syms])\n\
      \        idx = 0\n        n_data = len(data)\n        \n        # Preamble (32)\
      \ + Header (28) = 60 symbols minimum\n        while idx + 60 <= n_data:\n  \
      \          window = data[idx : idx + 32]\n            mismatches = int(np.sum(window\
      \ != self.preamble))\n            \n            if mismatches <= 2:\n      \
      \          # Descramble 7 header bytes\n                header_raw = bytearray(self.symbols_to_bytes(data[idx\
      \ + 32 : idx + 60]))\n                for i in range(7):\n                 \
      \   header_raw[i] ^= int(WHITENING_KEY[i % len(WHITENING_KEY)])\n          \
      \      \n                magic, pkt_type, seq_num, payload_len = struct.unpack('>H\
      \ B H H', bytes(header_raw))\n                \n                if magic !=\
      \ 0x5AA5 or payload_len > 512:\n                    idx += 1\n             \
      \       continue\n                    \n                total_pkt_syms = 32\
      \ + 28 + (4 * payload_len) + 16\n                if idx + total_pkt_syms > n_data:\n\
      \                    break\n                    \n                # Descramble\
      \ payload bytes\n                payload_raw = bytearray(self.symbols_to_bytes(data[idx\
      \ + 60 : idx + 60 + 4 * payload_len]))\n                for j in range(len(payload_raw)):\n\
      \                    payload_raw[j] ^= int(WHITENING_KEY[(7 + j) % len(WHITENING_KEY)])\n\
      \                \n                # Descramble CRC bytes\n                crc_raw\
      \ = bytearray(self.symbols_to_bytes(data[idx + 60 + 4 * payload_len : idx +\
      \ total_pkt_syms]))\n                for k in range(4):\n                  \
      \  crc_raw[k] ^= int(WHITENING_KEY[(7 + payload_len + k) % len(WHITENING_KEY)])\n\
      \                \n                rx_crc = struct.unpack('>I', bytes(crc_raw))[0]\n\
      \                calc_crc = zlib.crc32(bytes(header_raw) + bytes(payload_raw))\
      \ & 0xFFFFFFFF\n                \n                if calc_crc == rx_crc:\n \
      \                   self.total_packets += 1\n                    self.last_seq\
      \ = seq_num\n                    msg = bytes(payload_raw).decode('utf-8', errors='replace')\n\
      \                    self.last_text = msg\n                    \n          \
      \          log_entry = f\"[{time.strftime('%H:%M:%S')}] [Pkt #{seq_num:05d}]\
      \ {msg}\"\n                    self.recent_messages.append(log_entry)\n    \
      \                \n                    if self.total_packets % 25 == 0 or self.total_packets\
      \ <= 5:\n                        print(f\"[RX QPSK] Received Pkt #{seq_num:05d}:\
      \ {msg} (CRC OK)\")\n                        \n                    if self.log_file:\n\
      \                        try:\n                            self.log_file.write(f\"\
      {log_entry}\\n\")\n                            if self.total_packets % 10 ==\
      \ 0:\n                                self.log_file.flush()\n              \
      \          except Exception:\n                            pass\n           \
      \                 \n                    idx += total_pkt_syms\n            \
      \    else:\n                    self.crc_errors += 1\n                    if\
      \ self.crc_errors % 25 == 0 or self.crc_errors <= 5:\n                     \
      \   print(f\"[RX QPSK WARNING] CRC Error on Pkt #{seq_num} (calc={hex(calc_crc)},\
      \ rx={hex(rx_crc)})\")\n                    idx += total_pkt_syms\n        \
      \    else:\n                idx += 1\n                \n        if idx < n_data:\n\
      \            self.buffer = data[idx:]\n        else:\n            self.buffer\
      \ = np.array([], dtype=np.uint8)\n            \n        if len(self.buffer)\
      \ > 10000:\n            self.buffer = self.buffer[-2000:]\n            \n  \
      \      return len(in_syms)\n\n    def stop(self):\n        if hasattr(self,\
      \ 'gui_timer') and self.gui_timer:\n            self.gui_timer.stop()\n    \
      \    if hasattr(self, 'log_file') and self.log_file:\n            try:\n   \
      \             self.log_file.flush()\n                self.log_file.close()\n\
      \            except Exception:\n                pass\n        return True\n"
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: QPSK Text Deframer & Qt GUI Display
    log_to_file: 'True'
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    _io_cache: ('Text Packet Deframer & GUI', 'blk', [('log_to_file', 'True')], [('0',
      'byte', 1)], [], 'Robust QPSK Text Packet Deframer, Descrambler, CRC32 Verifier
      & Qt GUI Display', ['log_to_file'])
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1392, 320.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: note_0
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: "======================================================================\n\
      \           QPSK RECEIVER SYNCHRONIZATION TUNING GUIDE\n======================================================================\n\
      \n1. COSTAS LOOP BANDWIDTH (costas_loop_bw):\n   - What it does:\n     Tracks\
      \ carrier phase and eliminates fine carrier frequency offset\n     between the\
      \ transmitter and receiver oscillators.\n   - How to adjust:\n     * HIGHER\
      \ (0.06 - 0.10):\n       Widens the frequency acquisition (pull-in) range. Crucial\
      \ when\n       operating at high RF frequencies (e.g., 2.85 GHz) where USRP\
      \ TCXO\n       crystal offsets are 5 kHz - 12 kHz.\n       * Symptom if too\
      \ low (< 0.04): Constellation fails to lock and\n         spins in 8 clusters\
      \ (dynamic phase slips across 45-deg boundaries).\n       * Symptom if too high\
      \ (> 0.15): Constellation clusters smear/blur\n         due to excessive phase\
      \ noise tracking.\n     * Recommendation:\n       Keep default at 0.07 - 0.08\
      \ for instant hardware capture.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\
      \n2. TIMING LOOP BANDWIDTH (timing_loop_bw):\n   - What it does:\n     Symbol\
      \ clock synchronization (Gardner TED in Symbol Sync block).\n     Finds the\
      \ exact optimal time instant to sample each symbol at 1 SPS.\n   - How to adjust:\n\
      \     * HIGHER (0.02 - 0.05):\n       Faster clock lock; tracks sudden sample-rate\
      \ clock drift.\n     * LOWER (0.005 - 0.015):\n       Minimizes timing jitter\
      \ and inter-symbol interference (ISI).\n     * Recommendation:\n       Keep\
      \ at 0.01. Only increase if constellation points spread radially\n       along\
      \ symbol transition trajectories.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\
      \n3. FLL BAND-EDGE BANDWIDTH (w in digital_fll_band_edge_cc):\n   - What it\
      \ does:\n     Performs coarse carrier frequency offset estimation by balancing\n\
      \     energy at the upper and lower Nyquist band edges (+/- (1+Alpha)*Rs/2).\n\
      \   - How to adjust:\n     * Set to 0.03 - 0.05 to rapidly pull in large initial\
      \ crystal offsets\n       before the signal reaches the Costas loop.\n     *\
      \ If set too low (0.01), convergence is sluggish, forcing the Costas\n     \
      \  loop to do all the heavy lifting.\n======================================================================"
    note: receiver tuning guide
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [536, 504.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
